{"subjectId":"python","id":"dunder-methods","title":"Magic (Dunder) Methods","group":"Object-Oriented Python","order":16,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Double-underscore methods let your objects plug into Python's syntax: printing, <code>==</code>, <code>len()</code>, <code>[]</code>, <code>for</code>, <code>+</code>, <code>with</code> and more.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-eye\"></i>Representation</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Money:\n    def __init__(self, amount, cur=\"INR\"):\n        self.amount, self.cur = amount, cur\n    def __repr__(self):                  # unambiguous, for developers\n        return f\"Money({self.amount!r}, {self.cur!r})\"\n    def __str__(self):                   # readable, for users\n        return f\"{self.amount:.2f} {self.cur}\"\n\nm = Money(250)\nprint(repr(m))        # Money(250, 'INR')\nprint(m)              # 250.00 INR\nprint([m])            # [Money(250, 'INR')]</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>Containers show their items with <code>repr()</code>. Always define <code>__repr__</code>; add <code>__str__</code> when a friendlier form helps.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-equal\"></i>Equality, hashing &amp; ordering</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>from functools import total_ordering\n\n@total_ordering\nclass Version:\n    def __init__(self, major, minor):\n        self.key = (major, minor)\n    def __eq__(self, other):\n        return isinstance(other, Version) and self.key == other.key\n    def __hash__(self):                   # equal objects must hash equally\n        return hash(self.key)\n    def __lt__(self, other):\n        return self.key &lt; other.key\n\nv1, v2 = Version(1, 2), Version(1, 10)\nprint(v1 &lt; v2, v1 &gt;= v2, v1 == Version(1, 2))   # True False True\nprint(len({v1, Version(1, 2)}))                  # 1</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>Defining <code>__eq__</code> without <code>__hash__</code> makes instances <strong>unhashable</strong> (Python sets <code>__hash__ = None</code>). If objects can change, don't make them hashable.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list\"></i>Container &amp; iteration protocols</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Playlist:\n    def __init__(self, *songs):\n        self._songs = list(songs)\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self._songs)\n    def __getitem__(self, i):             # enables p[i], slicing and iteration\n        return self._songs[i]\n    def __contains__(self, song):\n        return song in self._songs\n\np = Playlist(\"a\", \"b\", \"c\")\nprint(len(p), p[0], p[-1], \"b\" in p)      # 3 a c True\nprint(list(p), p[1:])                     # ['a', 'b', 'c'] ['b', 'c']</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-math\"></i>Operators &amp; callables</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Vec:\n    def __init__(self, x, y):\n        self.x, self.y = x, y\n    def __add__(self, o):\n        return Vec(self.x + o.x, self.y + o.y)\n    def __mul__(self, k):\n        return Vec(self.x * k, self.y * k)\n    def __abs__(self):\n        return (self.x ** 2 + self.y ** 2) ** 0.5\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return f\"Vec({self.x}, {self.y})\"\n\nclass Adder:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.n = n\n    def __call__(self, x):                # instances become callable\n        return x + self.n\n\nprint(Vec(1, 2) + Vec(3, 4), Vec(3, 4) * 2, abs(Vec(3, 4)))   # Vec(4, 6) Vec(6, 8) 5.0\nprint(Adder(10)(5))                                            # 15</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Calls</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>str(x)</code>, <code>repr(x)</code></td><td><code>__str__</code>, <code>__repr__</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>x == y</code>, <code>x &lt; y</code></td><td><code>__eq__</code>, <code>__lt__</code> (+ <code>__le__</code>, <code>__gt__</code>, <code>__ge__</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>len(x)</code>, <code>x[i]</code>, <code>v in x</code></td><td><code>__len__</code>, <code>__getitem__</code>, <code>__contains__</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>for v in x</code></td><td><code>__iter__</code> (then <code>__next__</code> on the iterator)</td></tr><tr><td><code>x + y</code>, <code>x * y</code></td><td><code>__add__</code>, <code>__mul__</code> (<code>__radd__</code> for <code>y + x</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>x()</code></td><td><code>__call__</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>with x:</code></td><td><code>__enter__</code>, <code>__exit__</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>bool(x)</code></td><td><code>__bool__</code>, falling back to <code>__len__</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>"}